        "original_id": "23939264-c105-552a-99d7-85b3be347e43",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Billy Nungesser, Kip Holden, John Bel Edwards, David Vitter, Bill Cassidy, Susan Collins\n- Events: Louisiana lieutenant gubernatorial election, 2015; Louisiana gubernatorial election, 2015\n- Roles: United States Senator for Louisiana, Louisiana senior senator\n- Projects: Patient Freedom Act of 2017\n- Concepts: Affordable Care Act\n\nFacts:\n- In the 2015 Louisiana lieutenant gubernatorial election, Billy Nungesser defeated Kip Holden.\n- In the 2015 Louisiana gubernatorial election, John Bel Edwards defeated David Vitter by a margin similar to Billy Nungesser’s victory over Kip Holden.\n- David Vitter served as United States Senator for Louisiana from 2005 to 2017.\n- On January 23, 2017, Susan Collins and Bill Cassidy proposed the Patient Freedom Act of 2017 as a United States healthcare plan to replace the Affordable Care Act.\n- Bill Cassidy became Louisiana’s senior senator when David Vitter retired in 2017.\n- David Vitter, born on May 3, 1961, is an American lobbyist, lawyer, and politician.",
